# skimap: data is ignored, but the source-data contract is tracked.
# national/ moved under input/ when the data tree was reorganized, so each
# level on the way down has to be re-included in turn - git will not
# re-include a file whose parent directory is still excluded.
!skimap/data/
skimap/data/*
!skimap/data/input/
skimap/data/input/*
!skimap/data/input/national/
skimap/data/input/national/*
!skimap/data/input/national/README.md

# tours.gpkg is the one input that is not reproducible - every other file
# under data/ rebuilds from the national sources, but the tours are hand
# digitized. It is small, so it is tracked despite the blanket *.gpkg rule.
# Each directory has to be re-included before the file can be: git will not
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded.
!skimap/data/tours/
skimap/data/tours/*
!skimap/data/tours/tours.gpkg

# Lab profiles, on the same argument as tours.gpkg: a profile is the record
# of an experiment - which tours, which parameters, and what it was asking -
# and it rebuilds from nothing. Everything else under data/test/lab/ is
# output and stays ignored.
!skimap/data/test/
skimap/data/test/*
!skimap/data/test/lab/
skimap/data/test/lab/*
!skimap/data/test/lab/profiles/

# The corridor review, on the same argument again - but more so. config.json
# is the record of which models a round compared, and review.json is the
# judgement itself: every pick a person made looking at the map, one tour at
# a time. Re-running the pipeline reproduces every other file in this repo;
# nothing reproduces this one. cache/ is rendered overlays and export/ is
# built from review.json, so both stay ignored.
!skimap/data/review/
skimap/data/review/*
!skimap/data/review/config.json
!skimap/data/review/review.json
